{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "reentrancy/a-task-an-async-hook-starts-has-its-floor-only-while-the-body-runs",
  "title": "A task an ASYNC hook's body starts, awaited or not, calls at the body's floor while the body runs; once the body is over, its calls are work of its own, at the depth of their own event and each on a budget of its own, while another hook of the same trigger still runs",
  "rules": [
    "§8.3",
    "§9.5.1"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-8.3-016",
    "RK-8.3-018",
    "RK-8.3-044"
  ],
  "notes": "max_chain_depth is 1: the cascade of go holds ten hook calls and its AFTER_BROADCAST bodies have the floor 1. While a's body waits at a-body, the task it started sends during, and the task it awaits sends awaited: both at the floor. b's body waits at a gate no step opens until its timeout cuts it; once hook_timeout is emitted, the task it started sends after eleven times, at depth 0 and each on its own budget, all delivered, while a's body still runs: on the cascade's budget of ten hook calls, they could not all be delivered. The body is over by its timeout here: a body that returned is not observed, since no step tells when an ASYNC body returns.",
  "setup": {
    "kit": {
      "max_chain_depth": 1
    },
    "channels": [
      {
        "id": "sms",
        "type": "sms",
        "category": "transport"
      },
      {
        "id": "ws",
        "type": "websocket",
        "category": "transport"
      }
    ],
    "rooms": [
      {
        "id": "room-1",
        "bindings": [
